        "confidence": 0.88,
        "sourceReliability": "HIGH",
        "classification": "RESTRICTED",
        "contentHash": "hash-1790587895395-ej1opy",
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "rawText": "[SYNTHETIC THREAT INTELLIGENCE INCIDENT REPORT - NOT A REAL EXPLOIT]\nThreat Actor: APT29 (Cozy Bear) and FIN7 Syndicate\nTechniques: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application), T1059 (Command and Scripting Interpreter)\nVulnerabilities: CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell / Spring Boot JNDI RCE)\nTarget Systems: Computer 14 (Employee Management, Java Spring Boot port 8080) and Computer 07\n\nSummary:\nTelemetry corroborates APT29 continuing exploitation of public-facing endpoints via T1190. Additionally, the group leverages command interpreter T1059 to trigger remote JNDI lookups via Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228) against Computer 14. \nClaim: Host Computer 14 remains vulnerable and unmitigated.",
        "extractedEntitiesCount": 9,
        "extractedRelationsCount": 12
      }
    ],
    [
      "CTI-DOC-003",
      {
        "documentId": "CTI-DOC-003",
        "title": "SYNTHETIC: Authoritative Security Patch Advisory & Mitigation Reconciliation",
        "source": "Vendor Emergency Security Bulletin & SRE Verification (Synthetic)",
        "sourceType": "ADVISORY",
        "publishedAt": "2026-09-27T09:31:35.390Z",
        "observedAt": "2026-09-27T09:31:35.390Z",
        "ingestedAt": "2026-09-28T09:31:35.398Z",
        "lastSeenAt": "2026-09-27T09:31:35.390Z",
        "confidence": 0.98,
        "sourceReliability": "HIGH",
        "classification": "PUBLIC",
        "contentHash": "hash-1790587895398-5a02nf",
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "rawText": "[SYNTHETIC VENDOR SECURITY ADVISORY & MITIGATION BULLETIN]\nVulnerability: CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell)\nMitigation: Mitigation-Java-14 (Autonomous JNDI Lookup Lockdown & Spring Security Patch)\nTarget System: Computer 14 (Employee Management)\n\nSummary & Contradiction Resolution:\nOfficial vendor advisory verifies that Computer 14 has enforced complete JNDI lookup disabling and log4j-core 2.17.1 security patches. \nContradiction Claim: Prior reports asserting Computer 14 is unmitigated are now SUPERSEDED. Host Computer 14 is fully patched, verified healthy, and immune to CVE-2021-44228.",
        "extractedEntitiesCount": 4,
        "extractedRelationsCount": 4
      }
    ],
